{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the BO1 repair at head 817036fb32c32d81651494121f7c3d44f662b019, tree da00b122, for child request 4c5c41d3 and review request f02fb4f2. Verdict: APPROVED.\n\nThe head adds three commits to the reviewed head e272eb7c. I read the note first, then the diff, against the six items of review e173282d and ruling f4495460. That review's findings on the kernel additions, the preserved pins, Membership9, the Rules14 and Directory22 path, creation and rendering stand.\n\n## Items of e173282d\n\n1. Commons publication. Resolved.\n   - The `destination@16` check tries the exact older family, then the exact Commons family: Directory22, Rules14 and Membership9. Pins can't mix, because each family is compared whole.\n   - `operations.ts` now selects the same check for `destination@16`. Without it, two native cases failed. This also corrects the operation path for the older unpublished family, whose rooms had the same gap.\n   - `application-publication.test.ts` runs the real publication case for three families, including a Commons room, and shows that the older check refuses the others.\n2. The Page. Resolved. A column is read only with `Object.hasOwn`, and `view.test.ts` covers the inherited names.\n3. The rolled-back head. Resolved. `loadCommons` marks the window unreadable when the history head precedes the summary's head, or conflicts with it at the same sequence.\n4. Redirects. Resolved. The driver's fetch sets `redirect: \"error\"`, including for health, and refuses a redirected reply before it touches a body or custody. The note says that this proves no actual 307 hop.\n5. Host-none site answer. Resolved. `site/host.ts` recognizes the Commons Directory, so that room answers `no-repository`.\n6. Kernel text. Resolved. Section 7 names `ReferenceValue`, `isReference` and `platform:membership@9` in `INVITATION_KEY_MEMBERSHIPS`, each with a reason.\n\n## Ruling f4495460\n\n- Reference fields. Resolved. `requireReferenceInstall` runs for each definition in a package, on all three install proofs, after whole-definition validation. It finds a reference in item values, item refs, act fields and receive fields, including through lists and records. An older Rules refuses with the named `reference-requires-rules14`. Only the exact Rules14 pin opts in, so a later Rules must opt in deliberately. That is stricter than \"or later\", and the note and section 7 say so. A Rules10 negative and a Rules14 positive case exist.\n- `host.requires`. Resolved. The canonical order is required, and the reverse is refused without sorting.\n- Documents and configuration. Resolved. The ineffective Commons `DEMO_START_CONFIG` step is gone, `docs/security/trust-boundaries.md` has a `dap-commons` section, `demo-config.test.ts` pins the Commons configuration, and both scope-index files carry the new versions. The manifest binds each runner unit once.\n- Follow-ups. Section 7 records the fixed-slot reading of references. The 64-by-512 positive case and the lineage negatives exist. The note names the `notesAbout` measurement for BO2, per-member limits for BO3, and hosted complete-text and step coverage as owed before W1.\n\n## The gates\n\n- Gates 1 to 5 stay failed, and gates 6 and 7 stay historical passes for their own sources.\n- Gate 8 at d08a13e1, tree 12534bb5, passes all five stages. Its receipt exits 0 with complete capture, the same head and tree before and after, and no dropped bytes. Plain passes 3,177 with one skip and Native 871 with two skips.\n- From d08a13e1 to the head, only the note and the manifest change.\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- The worktree is clean. `git merge-tree --write-tree` onto main 5068dab4 gives 4615888c, with no conflict.\n- The 120 artifacts name exactly the 120 changed paths, all at this head, with the note first.\n- I ran the owning files once each, with no whole suite: plain `forms-reference`, `client/commons`, `mcp/commons`, `describe`, `view` and `application-package-v2`, 40 of 40; native `commons`, `commons-install`, `commons-bill`, `site-host` and `application-publication`, 15 of 15; `witness.test.mjs`, 4 of 4; `security-entry-points.test.mjs`, 10 of 10. The builder worktree stayed clean.\n- `node scripts/check-kernel-boundary.mjs` checks 126 production sources with no refusals.\n- The evidence verifies. The directory has 2,571 files and 409,914,975 bytes, its `SHA256SUMS` reruns clean, and no file is unlisted or writable. The external full manifest has SHA-256 6a1d85f2, and all 2,571 of its rows match. The committed manifest is now 33,936 bytes.\n- check-doc-links on an export of the head: 774 links, 0 broken. check-notes: 0 warnings. check-commit-messages: 11 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check`: clean.\n\n## Points that do not block\n\n1. The note still says \"Root\" in three lines, which the ruling asked to replace with plain words.\n2. The landing must take account of the documentation rewrite, which is under changes requested. Both heads edit `docs/kernel.md`, `docs/mcp.md`, `docs/deploy.md` and the security pages, so whichever lands second merges by hand. The planner chooses the order.\n3. `docs/deploy.md` keeps the words \"remains in the file as historical deployment custody\" for `DEMO_START_CONFIG`. That reads as status, but it's accurate.\n4. The `operations.ts` change affects running rooms on `destination@16` once deployed: a publication that used to stay refused can now be confirmed. It's the intended behaviour, and the deploy report should mention it.\n\n## Architecture\n\nEach family is compared whole, the reference gate sits at the install proofs, and the kernel keeps only shape. The landing adds a Worker configuration that stays closed until the planner binds its register. Approved.\n\n## Security\n\nA citation still grants nothing. Older rooms refuse a reference field by name. A note can no longer break the screen, a rolled-back head no longer reads as complete, and a redirect can't carry a signed envelope away. Approved.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThe repairs are small, and one helper holds the reference gate for all three proofs. Approved.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- The request's checks: all six items of e173282d and the ruling's additions hold, each with its case. Disposition of e173282d: resolved.\n- This approves source readiness only. Parent 41f77a01 stays open for hosted W1, which needs `dap-commons` provisioned, a complete-text read in the hosted tool, and the deployment.\n\nThe landing check will follow the landing. The head changes Worker code, so the planner decides on the deploy under its order.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f39e06ae80e79e734a8264ff950c30e601bd4300","binding":"assigned","head":"817036fb32c32d81651494121f7c3d44f662b019","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:72ad79c798a7040d1e560d0c75890e5163a974dd\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:614c265aff0dd7168ccc9ba3bce259f795669fcb\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0790129efe51158f9239fc92d51288166d6843d8","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}